requirements:
Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, Data Science, or a related field;
3+ years of industry experience in software engineering/machine learning;
Strong Python skills and hands-on experience with tabular processing libraries (Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-Learn, PySpark/Polars) and GBDT frameworks (XGBoost, LightGBM, CatBoost);
In-depth understanding of the complete modeling lifecycle: data gathering, feature engineering, hyperparameter tuning, model serving, and post-deployment monitoring;
Proficiency in PyTorch or TensorFlow for building custom neural architectures and tabular deep learning models;
Ability to read, reproduce, and extend recent research papers;
Strong analytical, problem-solving, and cross-functional collaboration skills.

